<% content_for :title, "Privacy Policy - Mezzanine" %>

<main class="legal">
  <article class="legal-content">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated August 31, 2026</p>

    <p>
      Mesa Workspace, Lda., trading as Mezzanine ("Mezzanine", "we" or "our"), operates this website
      and our coworking spaces. This policy explains, in simple terms, what personal data we collect,
      why, and what your rights are.
    </p>

    <p>
      We are the data controller for your personal data. Our registered office is at Rua Brito e Cunha,
      n.º 27, R/C, Matosinhos, Portugal. For any questions, contact us at
      <%= link_to "hello@mezzaninecowork.com", "mailto:hello@mezzaninecowork.com" %>.
    </p>

    <p>We collect information in three ways:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Data you provide directly:</strong> your name, email, and any message or comment you send us;
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Data collected automatically:</strong> when you browse our website, we log technical
        information such as your IP address, browser type, operating system, pages visited, and date and
        time of your visit. We also use analytics tools to understand how our website is used;
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Account and payment data:</strong> if you create an account or book our services, we store
        your profile and payment details (processed through our payment provider).
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      We do not collect sensitive data (such as ethnic origin, political opinions, religious beliefs,
      health data or sexual orientation). Please avoid including this type of information in any message
      you send us.
    </p>

    <p>We process your data based on the following legal grounds:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Consent:</strong> for sending marketing communications by email. You can withdraw your
        consent at any time;
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legitimate interest:</strong> to improve our website and keep our systems secure. You can
        object at any time by contacting us;
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legal obligation:</strong> when required by law.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>We use your data to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Respond to your enquiries and provide information;</li>
      <li>Send marketing communications (promotions, news and initiatives);</li>
      <li>Share relevant news about Mezzanine.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      We do not sell your data. We only share it with trusted service providers (such as web hosting,
      payment processing or analytics) who act on our behalf and are required to protect your data.
    </p>

    <p>
      We keep your data only for as long as necessary to fulfil the purposes described above, or as
      required by law. When data is no longer needed, we securely delete or anonymize it.
    </p>

    <p>
      Our website uses cookies to improve your browsing experience and for analytics purposes. You can
      manage your cookie preferences through your browser settings.
    </p>

    <p>
      You have the right to access, correct, delete or limit the use of your data. You can also unsubscribe
      from our communications at any time by emailing
      <%= link_to "hello@mezzaninecowork.com", "mailto:hello@mezzaninecowork.com" %>
      or clicking the unsubscribe link in our emails.
    </p>

    <p>
      To exercise your rights, we need to confirm your identity. We will respond within 30 days.
    </p>

    <p>
      If you are not satisfied with how we handle your data, you have the right to lodge a complaint with
      the Portuguese Data Protection Authority (CNPD) or another supervisory authority.
    </p>

    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. Any changes will be posted on this page with an updated
      revision date.
    </p>
  </article>
</main>
